  "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in {R}_{0}^{+}:9{x}^{2}+4\\le 4}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The elements of the given set are the positive real numbers and zero that satisfy the inequality $9{x}^{2}+4\\le 4.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+4 & \\le 4 \\\\ 9{x}^{2} & \\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\le 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution to the inequality above that is in ${R}_{0}^{+}$ is $x=0.$ Therefore, $A={0}.$",
